  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the functional representations of our two transformations:\n\n- A shift of $7$ units down can be represented by the function \n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(x,y-7).\n$$\n\n- A reflection across the line $y=x$ can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(y,x).\n$$\n\nLet's apply the given transformations to the point $P$ using our functions:\n\nFirst, we apply the shift. The image of the point $(-21,17)$ under the shift is\n\n$$\n(-21,17)↦(-21,17-7)=(-21,10).\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we apply the reflection. The image of the point $(-21,10)$ under the reflection is\n\n$$\n(-21,10)↦(10,-21).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resulting point is $(10,-21).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
